AYSH"],["they","eles / elas","EH-lsh / EH-lahsh"],["you (formal)","o senhor / a senhora","oo seh-NYOR / ah seh-NYOH-rah"]],"ex":[["I am a student","eu sou estudante","EH-oo soh shtoo-DAHN-t"],["you are tall","tu és alto","too ehsh AHL-too"],["she is my sister","ela é minha irmã","EH-lah eh MEEN-yah eer-MAHN"],["we are friends","nós somos amigos","nohsh SOH-moosh ah-MEE-goosh"],["they are teachers","eles são professores","EH-lsh sown proo-feh-SOH-rsh"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Most plurals add -s: casa → casas. Words ending in a consonant add -es. Words in -ão change: pão → pães, mão → mãos, limão → limões. Words in -l change: animal → animais. Articles change: o → os, a → as, um → uns, uma → umas."],"rows":[["the (m / f)","o / a","oo / ah"],["the (plural)","os / as","oosh / ahsh"],["a (m / f)","um / uma","oom / OO-mah"],["add -s","casa → casas","KAH-zahsh"],["add -es (consonant)","flor → flores","FLOH-rsh"],["-ão changes","pão → pães","paynsh"]],"ex":[["one cat, two cats","um gato, dois gatos","oom GAH-too doysh GAH-toosh"],["the book, the books","o livro, os livros","oo LEE-vroo oosh LEE-vroosh"],["a girl, girls","uma rapariga, raparigas","OO-mah rah-pah-REE-gah rah-pah-REE-gahsh"],["the flower, the flowers","a flor, as flores","ah flor ahsh FLOH-rsh"],["the bread, the loaves","o pão, os pães","oo pown oosh paynsh"]]},{"id":"ser-to-be-who-or-what","title":"Ser: to be (who or what)","text":["Ser: identity, origin, jobs, descriptions, time."],"rows":[["I am","eu sou","soh"],["you are","tu és","ehsh"],["he / she is","ele / ela é","eh"],["we are","nós somos","SOH-moosh"],["you all are","vocês são","sown"],["they are","eles / elas são","sown"]],"ex":[["I am English","sou inglês","soh een-GLAYSH"],["he is a doctor","ele é médico","EH-l eh MEH-dee-koo"],["it is Monday","é segunda-feira","eh seh-GOON-dah FAY-rah"],["we are from Uzbekistan","somos do Uzbequistão","SOH-moosh doo ooz-beh-keesh-TOWN"],["they are tall","eles são altos","EH-lsh sown AHL-toosh"]]},{"id":"estar-to-be-where-or-how","title":"Estar: to be (where or how)","text":["Estar: places and temporary states."],"rows":[["I am","eu estou","shTOH"],["you are","tu estás","shTAHSH"],["he / she is","ele / ela está","shTAH"],["we are","nós estamos","shTAH-moosh"],["they are","eles / elas estão","shTOWN"]],"ex":[["I am at home","estou em casa","shTOH ayn KAH-zah"],["she is tired","ela está cansada","EH-lah shTAH kahn-SAH-dah"],["where are you?","onde estás?","OHN-d shTAHSH"],["we are well","estamos bem","shTAH-moosh bayn"],["the soup is cold","a sopa está fria","ah SOH-pah shTAH FREE-ah"]]},{"id":"ter-to-have","title":"Ter: to have","text":["Ter is also used for age and feelings: tenho dezasseis anos, tenho fome, tenho sede."],"rows":[["I have","eu tenho","TAYN-yoo"],["you have","tu tens","taynsh"],["he / she has","ele / ela tem","tayn"],["we have","nós temos","TEH-moosh"],["they have","eles / elas têm","tayn"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","tenho um irmão","TAYN-yoo oom eer-MOWN"],["she has two cats","ela tem dois gatos","EH-lah tayn doysh GAH-toosh"],["we have time","temos tempo","TEH-moosh TAYM-poo"],["I am hungry","tenho fome","TAYN-yoo FOH-m"],["they have a car","eles têm um carro","EH-lsh tayn oom KAH-roo"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Three families: -ar, -er, -ir. Drop the ending, add the new one. Falar (to speak):"],"rows":[["eu","falo","FAH-loo"],["tu","falas","FAH-lahsh"],["ele / ela","fala","FAH-lah"],["nós","falamos","fah-LAH-moosh"],["eles / elas","falam","FAH-lown"]],"ex":[["I speak English","falo inglês","FAH-loo een-GLAYSH"],["you eat a lot","comes muito","KOH-mehsh MWEEN-too"],["she lives in Lisbon","ela vive em Lisboa","EH-lah VEE-v ayn leezh-BOH-ah"],["we work every day","trabalhamos todos os dias","trah-bahl-YAH-moosh TOH-doosh oosh DEE-ahsh"],["they drink water","bebem água","BEH-bayn AH-gwah"]]},{"id":"ir-to-go","title":"Ir: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: ir + infinitive. Vou comer = I am going to eat."],"rows":[["I go","eu vou","voh"],["you go","tu vais","vysh"],["he / she goes","ele / ela vai","vy"],["we go","nós vamos","VAH-moosh"],["they go","eles / elas vão","vown"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","vou para a escola","voh PAH-rah ah shKOH-lah"],["where are you going?","para onde vais?","PAH-rah OHN-d vysh"],["we are going to eat","vamos comer","VAH-moosh koo-MEHR"],["she is going to travel","ela vai viajar","EH-lah vy vee-ah-ZHAR"],["let's go!","vamos!","VAH-moosh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, rest. The adjective usually comes after the noun and agrees with it. You can drop the pronoun."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Como pão.","KOH-moo pown"],["adjective after noun","uma casa grande","OO-mah KAH-zah GRAHN-d"],["add time or place at the end","Trabalho aqui hoje.","trah-BAHL-yoo ah-KEE OH-zh"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","como pão","KOH-moo pown"],["Maria reads a book","a Maria lê um livro","ah mah-REE-ah leh oom LEE-vroo"],["we live in a big house","vivemos numa casa grande","vee-VEH-moosh NOO-mah KAH-zah GRAHN-d"],["he works here today","ele trabalha aqui hoje","EH-l trah-BAHL-yah ah-KEE OH-zh"],["the dog is black","o cão é preto","oo cown eh PREH-too"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put não before the verb. Double negatives are normal: não tenho nada.","Put não before the verb: eu não falo. Double negatives are normal: não tenho nada (I do not have anything). nada = nothing, ninguém = nobody, nunca = never."],"rows":[["not","não + verb","nown"],["nothing","nada","NAH-dah"],["nobody","ninguém","neen-GAYN"],["never","nunca","NOON-kah"],["não + verb","não falo","nown FAH-loo"],["nothing","nada","NAH-dah"],["nobody","ninguém","neen-GAYM"],["never","nunca","NOON-kah"]],"ex":[["I want","eu quero","EH-oo KEH-roo"],["I do not want","eu não quero","EH-oo nown KEH-roo"],["I speak English","falo inglês","FAH-loo een-GLEHSH"],["I do not speak English","não falo inglês","nown FAH-loo een-GLEHSH"],["I like it","gosto","GOHSH-too"],["I do not like it","não gosto","nown GOHSH-too"],["she is here","ela está aqui","EH-lah shTAH ah-KEE"],["she is not here","ela não está aqui","EH-lah nown shTAH ah-KEE"],["I have a car","tenho um carro","TEHN-yoo oom KAH-hoo"],["I do not have a car","não tenho carro","nown TEHN-yoo KAH-hoo"],["I understand","eu percebo","EH-oo per-SEH-boo"],["I do not understand","não percebo","nown per-SEH-boo"],["we are tired","estamos cansados","shTAH-moosh kahn-SAH-doosh"],["we are not tired","não estamos cansados","nown shTAH-moosh kahn-SAH-doosh"],["he works on Sundays","ele trabalha aos domingos","EH-l trah-BAH-lyah owsh doo-MEEN-goosh"],["he does not work on Sundays","ele não trabalha aos domingos","EH-l nown trah-BAH-lyah owsh doo-MEEN-goosh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: same words as a statement, with a rising voice. Or add \"não é?\" (isn't it?)."],"rows":[["statement","Falas inglês.","FAH-lahsh een-GLAYSH"],["question","Falas inglês?","FAH-lahsh een-GLAYSH"],["add \"right?\"","não é?","nown eh"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","falas inglês?","FAH-lahsh een-GLAYSH"],["is she a doctor?","ela é médica?","EH-lah eh MEH-dee-kah"],["do you have a pen?","tens uma caneta?","taynsh OO-mah kah-NEH-tah"],["are you tired?","estás cansado?","shTAHSH kahn-SAH-doo"],["is it far?","é longe?","eh LOHN-zh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","o que","oo k"],["who","quem","kayn"],["where","onde","OHN-d"],["when","quando","KWAHN-doo"],["why","porquê","poor-KEH"],["how","como","KOH-moo"],["which","qual","kwahl"],["how much / how many","quanto / quantos","KWAHN-too / KWAHN-toosh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","o que é isto?","oo k eh EESH-too"],["who is she?","quem é ela?","kayn eh EH-lah"],["where do you live?","onde moras?","OHN-d MOH-rahsh"],["when is the exam?","quando é o exame?","KWAHN-doo eh oo ee-ZAH-m"],["why are you late?","porque chegas tarde?","poor-K SHEH-gahsh TAR-d"],["how much is it?","quanto custa?","KWAHN-too KOOSH-tah"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","o meu / a minha","oo MEH-oo / ah MEEN-yah"],["your (informal)","o teu / a tua","oo TEH-oo / ah TOO-ah"],["his / her","o seu / a sua","oo SEH-oo / ah SOO-ah"],["our","o nosso / a nossa","oo NOH-soo / ah NOH-sah"],["their","o seu / a sua","oo SEH-oo / ah SOO-ah"]],"ex":[["my house","a minha casa","ah MEEN-yah KAH-zah"],["your friends","os teus amigos","oosh TEH-oosh ah-MEE-goosh"],["his sister","a irmã dele","ah eer-MAHN DEH-l"],["our teacher","o nosso professor","oo NOH-soo proo-feh-SOR"],["my mother","a minha mãe","ah MEEN-yah mayn"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["tu / teu for friends and family. o senhor / a senhora, with the he / she verb form, for strangers and work."],"rows":[["you, informal","tu","too"],["you, formal (m / f)","o senhor / a senhora","oo seh-NYOR / ah seh-NYOH-rah"],["your, informal","teu / tua","TEH-oo / TOO-ah"],["your, formal","seu / sua","SEH-oo / SOO-ah"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","tu falas","too FAH-lahsh"],["you speak (formal, to a man)","o senhor fala","oo seh-NYOR FAH-lah"],["how are you? (informal)","como estás?","KOH-moo shTAHSH"],["how are you? (formal)","como está?","KOH-moo shTAH"],["thank you, sir","obrigado, senhor","oh-bree-GAH-doo seh-NYOR"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past (simple): -ei, -aste, -ou, -ámos, -aram for -ar verbs. Future: ir + infinitive, or infinitive + -ei, -ás, -á, -emos, -ão."],"rows":[["I spoke","falei","fah-LAY"],["you spoke","falaste","fah-LAHSH-t"],["he / she spoke","falou","fah-LOH"],["I will speak","falarei","fah-lah-RAY"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","ontem trabalhei","OHN-tayn trah-bahl-YAY"],["she bought a book","ela comprou um livro","EH-lah kohm-PROH oom LEE-vroo"],["I went home","fui para casa","fwee PAH-rah KAH-zah"],["I will call you tomorrow","vou ligar-te amanhã","voh lee-GAR-t ah-mahn-YAHN"],["we will eat at eight","vamos comer às oito","VAH-moosh koo-MEHR ahsh OY-too"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal (tu): -ar verbs use the ele form (fala), -er / -ir verbs too (come, escreve). Negative: não + the -es / -as form (não fales). Formal (o senhor): fale, coma."],"rows":[["speak! (tu)","fala!","FAH-lah"],["do not speak!","não fales!","nown FAH-lehsh"],["speak! (formal)","fale!","FAH-l"]],"ex":[["come here","vem cá","vehm kah"],["do not come here","não venhas cá","nown VEHN-yahsh kah"],["sit down","senta-te","SEHN-tah-t"],["do not sit down","não te sentes","nown t SEHN-tehsh"],["be quiet","cala-te","KAH-lah-t"],["do not be late","não chegues atrasado","nown SHEH-gehsh ah-trah-ZAH-doo"],["open the door","abre a porta","AH-br ah POR-tah"],["close the window","fecha a janela","FEH-shah ah zhah-NEH-lah"],["listen to me","ouve-me","OH-v-m"],["do not worry","não te preocupes","nown t preh-oh-KOO-pehsh"],["speak slowly","fala devagar","FAH-lah deh-vah-GAR"],["wait a moment","espera um momento","shPEH-rah oom moh-MEHN-too"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["poder (can), dever / ter de (must), querer (want) + infinitive: posso nadar, tenho de ir, quero comer. Não deves = you must not."],"rows":[["I can","posso","POH-soo"],["I must","tenho de","TEHN-yoo d"],["I want","quero","KEH-roo"]],"ex":[["I can swim","sei nadar","say nah-DAR"],["I cannot swim","não sei nadar","nown say nah-DAR"],["can you help me?","podes ajudar-me?","POH-dehsh ah-zhoo-DAR-m"],["we must go","temos de ir","TEH-moosh d eer"],["we must not go","não devemos ir","nown deh-VEH-moosh eer"],["I want to eat","quero comer","KEH-roo koh-MEHR"],["I do not want to eat","não quero comer","nown KEH-roo koh-MEHR"],["you can come","podes vir","POH-dehsh veer"],["you cannot come","não podes vir","nown POH-dehsh veer"],["she wants to study","ela quer estudar","EH-lah kehr shtoo-DAR"],["I must work today","tenho de trabalhar hoje","TEHN-yoo d trah-bah-LYAR OH-zh"],["you must not run","não deves correr","nown DEH-vehsh koh-HEHR"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["em = in / on / at; sobre / em cima de = on; debaixo de = under; ao lado de = next to; perto de = near; às nove = at nine."],"rows":[["on","em cima de","ehm SEE-mah d"],["under","debaixo de","deh-BAH-ee-shoo d"],["next to","ao lado de","ow LAH-doo d"],["near","perto de","PEHR-too d"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","o livro está em cima da mesa","oo LEE-vroo shTAH ehm SEE-mah dah MEH-zah"],["the cat is under the table","o gato está debaixo da mesa","oo GAH-too shTAH deh-BAH-ee-shoo dah MEH-zah"],["I am at school","estou na escola","shTOH nah shKOH-lah"],["I am at home","estou em casa","shTOH ehm KAH-zah"],["the shop is next to the bank","a loja fica ao lado do banco","ah LOH-zhah FEE-kah ow LAH-doo doo BAHN-koo"],["the park is near the station","o parque fica perto da estação","oo PAR-k FEE-kah PEHR-too dah shtah-SOWN"],["we meet in the morning","encontramo-nos de manhã","ehn-kohn-TRAH-moo-noosh d mahn-YAH"],["the lesson is at nine","a aula é às nove","ah OW-lah eh ahsh NOH-v"],["the key is in the bag","a chave está na mala","ah SHAH-v shTAH nah MAH-lah"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["mais + adjective + (do) que = more than (mais alto do que eu). menos... que = less than. o mais... = the most. melhor = better, pior = worse."],"rows":[["bigger than","maior que","mah-ee-OR k"],["better","melhor","meh-LYOR"],["the biggest","o maior","oo mah-ee-OR"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","grande, maior, o maior","GRAHN-d mah-ee-OR oo mah-ee-OR"],["small, smaller, the smallest","pequeno, mais pequeno, o mais pequeno","peh-KEH-noo mighsh peh-KEH-noo oo mighsh peh-KEH-noo"],["this is better than that","isto é melhor do que aquilo","EESH-too eh meh-LYOR doo k ah-KEE-loo"],["this is worse than that","isto é pior do que aquilo","EESH-too eh pee-OR doo k ah-KEE-loo"],["she is taller than me","ela é mais alta do que eu","EH-lah eh mighsh AHL-tah doo k EH-oo"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Tashkent é maior do que Samarcanda","tahsh-KEHNT eh mah-ee-OR doo k sah-mar-KAHN-dah"],["it is the cheapest","é o mais barato","eh oo mighsh bah-RAH-too"],["the same as","igual a","ee-GWAHL ah"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","ele é professor","EH-l eh proh-feh-SOR"],["you (plural) are students","vocês são estudantes","voh-SEHSH sown shtoo-DAHN-tsh"],["I am happy","estou feliz","shTOH feh-LEESH"],["she is at school","ela está na escola","EH-lah shTAH nah shKOH-lah"],["you are my friend","és o meu amigo","ehsh oo MEH-oo ah-MEE-goo"],["it is cold","está frio","shTAH FREE-oo"],["I study English","estudo inglês","shTOO-doo een-GLEHSH"],["he teaches maths","ele ensina matemática","EH-l ehn-SEE-nah mah-teh-MAH-tee-kah"],["they work every day","eles trabalham todos os dias","EH-lsh trah-BAH-lyown TOH-doosh oosh DEE-ahsh"],["is this your book?","este é o teu livro?","EHSH-t eh oo TEH-oo LEE-vroo"],["are they here?","eles estão aqui?","EH-lsh shTOWN ah-KEE"],["do you like tea?","gostas de chá?","GOHSH-tahsh d shah"],["what time is it?","que horas são?","k OH-rahsh sown"],["whose book is this?","de quem é este livro?","d kayn eh EHSH-t LEE-vroo"],["how old are you?","quantos anos tens?","KWAHN-toosh AH-noosh tayns"],["how do you say it?","como se diz?","KOH-moo s deesh"],["your book (formal)","o seu livro","oo SEH-oo LEE-vroo"],["their house","a casa deles","ah KAH-zah DEH-lsh"],["my phone","o meu telemóvel","oo MEH-oo teh-leh-MOH-vehl"],["excuse me, sir","com licença, senhor","kohm lee-SEHN-sah sehn-YOR"],["please sit down (formal)","sente-se, por favor","SEHN-t-s poor fah-VOR"],["come here (informal)","vem cá","vehm kah"],["yesterday I was tired","ontem estava cansado","OHN-tehm shTAH-vah kahn-SAH-doo"],["I will study tomorrow","vou estudar amanhã","voh shtoo-DAR ah-mahn-YAH"],["we went to the park","fomos ao parque","FOH-moosh ow PAR-k"]]}],"name":"Portuguese","id":"pt","flag":"pt","note":""}